[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:71. A Famous Clock]
[00:00.380]Passage 71 | 文章七十一
[00:02.655]A famous clock. | 著名的时钟。
[00:05.505]When you visit London, | 当你游览伦敦时，
[00:08.610]one of the first things you will see is Big Ben, | 你首先会看到的大本钟，
[00:12.365]the famous clock which can be heard all over the world on the BBC. | 这座著名的时钟，在BBC上全世界都能听到它的声音。
[00:18.435]If the Houses of Parliament had not been burned down in 1834, | 如果议会大厦没有在1834年被烧毁，
[00:24.360]the great clock would never have been erected. | 这个大钟就永远不会被建造。
[00:28.340]Big Ben takes its name from Sir Benjamin Hall, | 大本钟的名字来源于本杰明·霍尔爵士，
[00:33.525]who was responsible for the making of the clock | 他负责制造这座钟，
[00:36.765]when the new Houses of Parliament were being built. | 当新的议会大厦正在建造时。
[00:41.430]It is not only of immense size, | 它不仅体型巨大，
[00:45.650]but is extremely accurate as well. | 而且非常准确。
[00:49.170]Officials from Greenwich Observatory | 格林威治天文台的官员
[00:52.505]have the clock checked twice a day. | 每天检查这座钟两次。
[00:55.780]On the BBC, | 在BBC上，
[00:57.870]you can hear the clock when it is actually striking, | 当它真正敲响时，你可以听到钟声，
[01:01.450]because microphones are connected to the clock tower. | 因为麦克风连接到钟楼上。
[01:06.765]Big Ben has rarely gone wrong. | 大本钟很少出问题。
[01:11.115]Once, however, | 然而有一次，
[01:13.035]it failed to give the correct time. | 它未能给出正确的时间。
[01:16.265]A painter who had been working on the tower | 一位在塔上工作的画家
[01:19.960]hung a pot of paint on one of the hands | 把一罐油漆挂在了其中一根指针上，
[01:23.770]and slowed it down. | 使它慢了下来。